WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:02.629 align:start position:0%
 
we all know that the straw hat's journey  through the grand line  is heavily dominated by violence this  violence is enacted by the various  antagonists and by the cruise battles  against them  being a shonen manga fighting is a  central element in the story of one  piece  and yet out of all the established straw  hats there is only one that  actually embraces this need for battle  and makes it a part of its ambitions and  philosophy  zorro is a fascinating character in many  ways  but it is undeniable that at his core he  is a warrior  as a true swordsman inside destroyed  crew he therefore rightfully holds the  position of the fighter  and yet i think that this position alone  does not satisfy the potential of this  man's unique and complex character  much rather it seems that zorro has been  introduced as the counterpartus captain  that is necessary in order to  successfully reach the top of the pirate  world  i would argue that right from the start  zorro has been luffy's right hand man  making him much more than just a simple  fighter on the crew zorro  is the straw hat's first mate now before  we look at the actions and the  characteristics of zorro that qualify  him for this position  let's first establish what the roles of  fighter and first mate really mean  and what sets them apart there is a  difference between being a fighter  and just being an aggressor it is easy  to push around those who are weaker and  enjoy imposing your power over someone  as you might realize there are many  aggressors in one piece and it is easy  to see  why we detest them so much a fighter is  different  fighting is when it's hard fighting  means going out of your comfort zone  it means not giving up it means hating  to lose but  learning from the experience anyway  fighting doesn't always involve violence  it simply means giving your all for  something by overcoming any obstacle in  the way  zoro without a doubt is a true fighter  he identifies himself by becoming  stronger  fighting for his dream to become the  greatest swordsman in the world  in any situation he gives it his all and  sometimes  even more zorro hates nothing more than  losing  but even in defeat he learns from his  failure and draws motivation  and strength from them but what sets him  apart from for example luffy  who's also a fighter in the very same  sense another meaning of fighting is  that of battle while luffy wants to get  stronger and faces off against  ever-strong opponents his true ambition  is to achieve  absolute freedom becoming strong is  therefore just a necessary requirement  that has to be fulfilled  at heart luffy only fights to resolve  conflict and to help others  zorro is different his ambition to  become the greatest swordsman in the  world  is built on a true passion for combat  his mindset  and worldview are centered around battle  and strength  we do not know how zorro came to think  that way but we only know that he  already strived for strength at a very  young age  while we know that zoro's character is  much more complex than this  it certainly can be said that at his  core he's a person that has built his  life around fighting  in other words zorro is a true fighter  through and through  what then is the position of the first  mate and why is sorrow more than just a  great fighter  usually a first mate is the top officer  on board a ship after the captain  famous examples of this are silva's  rayleigh the first mate of the roger  pirates  as well as ben beckman the first mate of  the red hair pirates  first mates can fill a number of roles  from checking stock to making sure  everyone else is doing their job on the  ship leaving their captain to more  important duties  since they are the second in command  they answer only to the captain of the  ship  essentially the first mate is the crew  member that the captain must put  full trust in and pick very carefully  they are the captain's right-hand man  and if the captain's not at hand the  first mate is the next in line to take  over the captain's job  now as you might be well aware of the  straw hats are no regular pirate crew  the members don't operate as much on  hierarchy and power  as they do on trust loyalty and  friendship towards another  additionally the crew is ridiculously  small especially  compared to any other major player in  the new world based on this one could  make the argument that the position of a  first mate or  any type of officer structure is not  really necessary inside the straw hats  this is also supported by the fact that  no kind of officer role has ever been  officially introduced for any of these  draw heads in the first place  and yet i think that oda has made it  very clear that  zorro is supposed to be luffy's right  hand since the straw heads are  unconventional in many ways  the same goes for the position of the  first mate on our hero's ship  it fulfills another purpose than on  other pirate crews  similar to shanks or roger luffy needs  someone who has a more realistic and  rational view on things than he does  someone that tells him a hard truth or  reminds him of what is really important  based on that some people argue that  nami might also be a good fit for this  role  but the first mate also needs to be  someone that can stand next to his  captain in battle  and invoke a similar level of respect  and authority  especially in the violent and  conflict-rich world of one piece  fighting strength is an important  feature for any captain's right hand  and as we already have established  previously zorro is without a doubt one  of the greatest fighters in the story  so let's look at the other qualities  that zorro has and  why they make him the only true fit for  the position of first mate  what makes him more than just a great  swordsman and a fighter on the crew  zorro is one of the most loved  characters in the show for a reason  while his characteristic 3-style sword  and his cool design  certainly play their part in this for  many people it goes  much deeper than this on the surface he  may seem cold  and distant he is not someone to show an  awful lot of emotion  and is rarely seen joking around with  his crewmates and yet being one of the  main characters in the series we have  learned a lot about zorro over the  course of the years that might not have  been obvious at first sight  so now let's look at three important  personality traits that qualify zorro  for the position of the first mate  the first trait that we will look at is  zoro's strong sense of honor  and loyalty having grown up under the  strict rules of a dojo  zorro has without a doubt developed a  mindset that revolves heavily around the  honor of a swordsman  he refuses to take any action that goes  against this honor  even if it means putting his own life on  the line this was established very early  on in the story  when zorro first faced off with dracul  mihawk his sense of loyalty towards his  captain  his crewmates as well as towards his  ideals is repeatedly shown in various  instances as well  the most drastic example of this is his  sacrifice for luffy on thriller bark  when taking on all of his captain's  damage to protect him from kuma  in other words zoro is the most loyal  and honorable straw hat that has stood  beside luffy from the very beginning  additionally he also strives to uphold  these ideals when  faced with the other member's actions  his appeal towards luffy to not take  back uso without an apology  as well as his criticism of sanji's  decision to leave the crew behind  show how important respect and loyalty  toward his captain are to him  this makes him the only one in the crew  that actively tries to build luffy's  authority  so that his captain's orders are  respected when a critical situation  arises  the second personality trait that is  often overlooked within sorrow is his  kindness and empathy  despite his cold and harsh appearance  zoro actually holds strong ideals of  morality and has a very kind heart  while he would do anything for any of  his crewmates that he values very dearly  he has also repeatedly proven to care  about strangers that are in need of help  he carried a man shot by a celestial  dragon carlos to the hospital to save  his life  and just recently he defended princess  yori and her companion toko against one  of the shogun's assassins in wano  even while fighting another opponent not  only are kindness and empathy  defining traits of this draw-head crew  but zoro also has the power to act on it  and defend his nakama as well as people  in need  he knows what the right thing is to do  and always stands close to luffy to  bring down those who bring injustice to  the world  lastly being a true fighter sorrow has a  certain degree of ruthlessness and  realism that are necessary to survive in  the grand line and that is captain lags  while the straw hats are the heroes of  our story due to their positivity and  caring nature  sometimes they can be seen as nivity  sorrow might very well be the only  member that is able to do what is  necessary to ensure his comrade safety  and survival  unlike some of the members of the crew  zoro does not shrink from the idea of  using deadly force against dangerous  enemies  and is known to have killed even before  joining luffy additionally he also has a  more realistic and darker view of the  world  while luffy's optimism and positive  leadership style have brought the crew  very far on their journey  it is nonetheless important to have a  perspective in the crew  that sees the things as they are in this  sense zorro perfectly completes his  captain by bringing the necessary  seriousness with him that has saved the  straw hats more than once  these three traits honor and loyalty  kindness and empathy as well as  ruthlessness and realism make zoro the  only suitable candidate for the man  standing beside the next pirate king  beside these three characteristics there  is also soros relationship with luffy  as mentioned before zoro would do  anything for his captain  and respect luffy really deeply as the  first member of the crew  he is what really was to roger a partner  that stands side by side with his leader  through every situation  when it comes to any critical situation  luffy and zoro don't need a lot of  communication to know exactly what they  have to do  additionally while zoro might not  officially be his first mate  it's very clear that he's seen that way  from the outside not only does  bartolomeo name him as such  he was also the only member of the crew  that entered the group of the supernova  with luffy  and of course he is the man who will  become the strongest swordsman in the  world

